course: dictionary
lesson: 1246
title: Bunny and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bunny is a child's or friendly word for a rabbit, especially a young or small one. In «Poppy hugs her new bunny», the word is soft and loving, and it means a pet rabbit.
explain: Bunny has other meanings too. In the Easter Bunny it is a character in a story who brings chocolate eggs, and in «gym bunny» it means someone who loves the gym. On a ski slope, the bunny slope is an easy hill for beginners.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about carrots and hugs, it is a rabbit. If it is about snow and skis, it is a beginner's hill. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A bunny is a child's or friendly word for a rabbit, especially a young or small one.
fact: The Easter Bunny is a fun character in a story who brings chocolate eggs.
fact: A «gym bunny» is someone who loves the gym.
fact: A bunny slope is an easy hill for beginners in skiing (US); in the UK it is called a nursery slope.
fact: Real wild rabbits fill up on grass, clover and leafy plants; carrots are only a small, sugary treat.
exercise: «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces that Snowy gets a carrot every day.» What is a bunny here? | A small bird | A type of carrot | *A pet rabbit | A hill for skiing
exercise: Lily says she is a «gym bunny» because she goes to the gym every day. What does gym bunny mean? | A kind of exercise mat | A rabbit that lives in a gym | *Someone who loves the gym | A ski slope for beginners
exercise: Which fact about real wild rabbits is true, from the text? | They only eat carrots, every day | *They fill up mostly on grass, clover and leafy plants | They eat chocolate eggs at Easter | They live in hospitals
test: On a ski trip the teacher says, «Stay on the bunny slope until you learn to stop.» Where should you ski? | *An easy hill for beginners | A rabbit hutch | A very steep mountain | The top of the chairlift
test: Bugs Bunny munches a carrot in every cartoon, so many people think carrots are what rabbits should eat. What does the text say is true? | Cartoons always show exactly what rabbits eat | Rabbits love carrots more than any other food | *Real rabbits eat mostly grass, and carrots are only a small treat | Carrots are a kind of grass
exam: Mia reads that workers wear full «bunny suits» in clean rooms, because one speck of dust can ruin a chip. What is a bunny suit here? | A soft, cute rabbit costume | A ski suit for beginners | A suit for the Easter Bunny | *A full protective suit that keeps dust away
